<title>USA: American Healthcorp Inc Q2 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>American Healthcorp Inc Q2 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>NASHVILLE, Tenn. 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr	   loss	 $0.02   profit	 $0.09</p>
<p> Oper Shr    loss	 $0.05   profit	 $0.06</p>
<p> Net	   loss	   194   profit	   705</p>
<p> Oper net    loss	   430   profit	   508</p>
<p> Revs			 7,353		    7,691</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   8,259		    8,155</p>
<p>	   6 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr	 profit$0.03	  profit  $0.19</p>
<p> Oper shr loss   $0.03	  profit  $0.15</p>
<p> Net	 profit269	    profit  1,505</p>
<p> Oper Net  loss  223	    profit  1,159</p>
<p> Revs		15,332		   15,714</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  8,229		     8,122</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Oper figures represent results of continuing operations and exclude discontinued operations.</p>
<p>Q2 earnings from discontinued operations were profit $0.03/shr vs profit $0.03, or profit $236,000 vs profit $197,000, and for six months profit $0.06 vs profit $0.04, or profit $492,000 vs profit $346,000.</p>
<p>American Healthcorp said it reported continuing and discontinued net income to include its announced spin-off of AmSurg Corp.</p>
<p>Q2 ended February 28.</p>
